http://www.statoids.com. This corresponds to \u201cThirdOrder\u201d and \u201cThirdLevel\u201dadministrative units at http://Geonames.organd http://www.gadm.orgrespectively", "", "Administrative division 4 for water point record based on GPS and GADM or HDX dataset boundaries. ", "", "", "Categorized version of the #status parameter. Based on terms from the #status entry, status_clean includes 5 categories: Fully functional, Functional but needs repair, Non functional and needs repair, Non functional due to dry season, Abandoned and Other. These categories will continue to evolve and will be refined in future updates. ", "", "Categorized facility type based on JMP definitions", "", "Cleaned/categorized version of raw #water_tech entries", "", "Cleaned/categorized version of raw #water_source entries", ": Provide the name of the entity or entities that installed the water system. Thisshould be the entities that completed or weredirectly responsible for the construction,ratherthan a donor or other involved stakeholder", "Provide the 4-digit installation year", "Provide the payment amount and basis (e.g. monthly, per jerry can, when broken,etc.). If no amount is provided, the basis can be provided alone. An amount without a paymentbasis cannot be included", "Provide a status ofthe physical/mechanical condition of thewater point", "Results of e. coli or thermotolerant coliform water quality test froma 100ml watersample collected directly from water point.Total coliform should not be included. Ifthermotolerant, must be noted in themetadata. Value should represent themost probable number or colony forming units in 100ml.", "Results of e. coli or thermotolerant coliform water quality test froma 100ml watersample collected directly from water point.Total coliform should not be included. Ifthermotolerant, must be noted in themetadata. Value should represent presence or absence.", "Information regarding the perceived quality of the water including taste,appearance, and/or odor", "Cleaned version of the #subjective_quality parameter", "Cleaned version of the #pay parameter. ", "Name of dataset associated with upload", "", "", "", "", "Provide the Unique ID for the specific water point infrastructure, as reported bydata collector. This could be a physical ID on the water point or an internal system ID.", "The identifier for asmall piped scheme that connects multiple individual waterpoints.", "This field can be used to incorporate any additional information not already part ofthe WPDx standard that is useful to the data provider.", " Provide the URL of a photograph of the water system. Multiple URLs can beincluded, with each URL separated by a semi-colon (;).", "Provide the public link to the data record for a specific water point or full data set,including any non-standard compliant data.", "", "Select the classification of the entity that directly manages the water point.", "", "Provide the name of the entity or entities that completed the most recentrehabilitation of the water system. Thisshould be the entities that complete or were directlyresponsible for the construction, ratherthan a donor or other involved stakeholder", "Provide the 4-digit year when the most recent major rehabilitation (not just regularmaintenance)occurred", "Row number", "Provide the name of the organization collecting the data record", "Provide the decimal value of the latitude in WGS 1984", "Provide the decimal value of the longitude in WGS 1984", "Provide the date that the data was collected", "Identify if any water is available on the day of the visit, recognizing that itmay be alimited flow", "Describe the water source (e.g. shallow well, spring, borehole, river, pond, etc.)", "Describe the system being used to transport the water from the source to the point of collection (e.g. Handpump (include manufacturer, i.e. Afridev, India Mark II, Malda, etc.), Kiosk, Tapstand, etc.).", "Country where water point is located"], "columns_format": [{}, {}, {}, {}, {}, {}